1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT JUAN PABLO MONTOYA, SON OF RAMON MONTOYA AND MARIA DOROTEA TRUJILLO
2 CONT In the marriages of Santa Cruz (not too far from Santa Clara is the followiing entry.
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Nov 1861 - After proclaiming the banns on three festive days (not listed), finding no impediments I married Juan Pablo Montoya, single, s/o Ramon Montoya, deceased and Maria Dorotea Trujillo, vecino from el Potrero with Maria D
2 CONC olores Sanches, single natural d/o Maria Concescion Sanches vecina from the same place, Wit: Marselo Bigil and Juan Nepomuseno Martines, vecinos from this jurisdiction, Off: Juan de Jesus Trujillo
2 CONT
2 CONT From Document Source: These marriages are from the Marriage Register of the Church of San Juan de Los Caballeros, Territory of New Mexico from August 6, 1857 through December 18, 1900. Microfilm No. 0016-979
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT August 10, 1905 - In this Church of San Juan the matrimony of Francisco Antonio Montoya de San Antonio de Chama son of Francisco Montoya and Maria Dolores de Herrera with Marina Martinez de San Antonio de Chama daughter of Antonio
2 CONC  Jose Martinez and Josefa Salazar.
2 CONT
2 CONT A fellow researcher
2 CONT Martha Sanchez-Wilson
