1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Hello, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the condensed version of our find, and what we
2 CONT
2 CONT will need to seal a long search.
2 CONT
2 CONT My Grandmother, Maria Juana Montolla, is the daugher of Juan Pablo Montoya and Maria Dolores Medina.  Albinita is Debbie'sMartinez' side of the family. Juanita and Albinita  Montolla/Montoya,are sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Pablo MONTOLLA
2 CONT
2 CONT Could be the son of Ramon Montoya and Maria Dolores Tujillo baptized 8 March 1835 at Santa Cruz De la Canada, Santa Fe, New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramon Montoya and Dorotea Trujillo. Their children were baptized at Santa Cruz De La Canada, Santa Fe. Their son
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Pablo Montoya was baptized 8 March 1835. He was married at the same church 10 November 1861 to Maria Dolores Sanchez.
2 CONT
2 CONT She could have been a young widow. We would need to see the original record on microfilm to see if that is the case.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Dolores Trujillo baptized, 8 March 1835, at Santa Cruz de la Canada, Santa Fe, New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT He could also be the son of Manuel Montoya and Meregilda Espinosa (baptized 4 July 1840) as Jose Paulo Montoya at Mission De San Lorenzo De Picuris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Montoya and Meregilda Espinosa. Their son Jose Paolo Montoya was baptized 4 July 1840. That record we saw at a data base in Colorado, said he married Maria Dolores Medina, daughter of Geronimo Medina and Maria Estefana Fres
2 CONC quis. No marriage data was provided.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen from Colorado City gave material on Juan Pablo Montoya born in 1864. According to Karen Moore, she states that Karen of Colorado had not checked the burial dates. It was a Jose Pablo
2 CONT
2 CONT Montoya that was born to Manual Montoya and Hermeregilda Espinosa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And he died six months after birth. Manuel Vincente de lose Dolores Montoya, bpt. 1 July 1792 and wife Hermenegilda Espinosa.
2 CONT
2 CONT She also does not think that Juan Pablo Montoya is descended from Ramon Montoya and Isabel Armenta. That particular Juan pablo married Maria Dolores (SANCHEZ). She found their marriage date in 1862 in Santa Cruz, but she did not c
2 CONC opy and send it to us. DO YOU HAVE THIS AVAILABLE. Her father was NOT Geronimo.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had a daughter Maria LIBRADA born in 1869 in Santa Cruz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deberah and I believe that the parents of Our Maria Dolores Medina are definately Geronimo and Maria Estefan Frequis. ( We have since changed our minds.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Taos Baptisms 1701-1860 Page 538 &amp;amp; 539. by Thomas D. Martinez.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was living in her father's house in 1860. This could mean he was married by this time. In 1880 Census, she was living inLlano, Taos, New Mexico FHL fILM 1254804, FILM T9-0804, Page 265A
2 CONT
2 CONT I found an entry in a 40 year CD I bought. Has some listing on
2 CONT
2 CONT Taos County marriages. On page 50, there is a mention of Fresquis, Antonio Jose, widow, and Fernandez, Maria Estefan, 25 March 1863 by Antonio Jose Martinez Page 6. Our Maria Estefana Fresquis is the mother of Maria Dolores Medina
2 CONC , who married Geronimo Medina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Names always give leads.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other source: Film or Fiche Number 0016964 1726-1956 Catholic
2 CONT
2 CONT Church, Holy Cross, Santa Fe, New Mexico. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deciding factor would be the marriage record for Juan Pablo or Jose Pablo Montoya/Montolla to Maria Dolores Medina. (We have the marriage record, it did not state who the parents of Pablo or Dolores was).
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage would probably would have occured in 1862. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage  any where from 1859 through 1863.  Maria Dolores Medina: 0016868 Source
2 CONT
