1 NAME Cruz /Granillo/
2 GIVN Cruz
2 SURN Granillo
2 _MARNM Valdez
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 MAY 1867
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 NOV 1961
2 ADDR
3 CITY Downey
3 STAE CA
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU See http://genforum.genealogy.com/valdez/messages/364.html
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From http://genforum.genealogy.com/valdez/messages/364.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname: Granillo Valdez 
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted by: Cecilia (ID *****5645) Date: April 25, 2002 at 22:15:32 
2 CONT    of 629  
2 CONT
2 CONT Does any one know of a Cruz Granillo? She married Jose Angel Valdez in El Paso, Texas, between 1884 and 1927. Her mother was Josefa Zambrano and her father was Antonio Granillo. She had a sister named Felicitas Granillo Zamora. Cr
2 CONC uz Granillo died in Downey, California (in the county of Los Angeles). This is all the info I have been able to find. If you can help, please contact me.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Re: Surname: Granillo Valdez
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted by: dwight brown (ID *****5269) Date: October 21, 2007 at 15:52:51
2 CONT
2 CONT In Reply to: Surname: Granillo Valdez by Cecilia  of 629  
2 CONT
2 CONT i looking for felicitas granillo born about 1860 in sonora mexico and died about 1920 in arizona, any relation please forward an email to me
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Re: Surname: Granillo Valdez
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted by: Leigh Cagilaba (ID *****0349) Date: September 30, 2008 at 13:57:22
2 CONT
2 CONT In Reply to: Surname: Granillo Valdez by Cecilia  of 629  
2 CONT
2 CONT Sorry to take so long in getting back to you. I only just stumbled upon your old posting from 2002.
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicitas Granillo Zamora was my great great grandmother and my mother just told me that she died in Las Cruces, NM but she'll have to look up the year. She (Felicitas) was married to Desiderios Zamora.
2 CONT
2 CONT My mother was born in Las Cruces but she and I both live in Washington State (she's currently visiting family in Colorado.) We never knew anything about Felicitas' parents or siblings though. My mother recently did one of those ne
2 CONC w "trace your ancestors" swab tests where a lab traces your genetic roots, and it came back that Felicitas' maternal blood line (through her mother, and her mother's mother, and her mother's mother, and so on) was from Central/Sou
2 CONC th America.)
2 CONT
2 CONT So I have to ask - are you related to Felicitas?
