3 CITY Las Cruces
3 STAE NM
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 MAR 1965
1 OCCU See http://www.familysearch.org/eng/search/frameset_search.asp?PAGE=/eng/search/ancestorsearchresults.asp
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Online memorial at http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=108386053
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicitas had a sister named Cruz, and their parents were Antonio Granillo and Josefa Zambrano (taken from the marriage certificate for Felicitas and Desiderio.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicitas had a wooden leg most of her life, of which she aquired when she was a young teenager.  There are two stories that have been passed down regarding why she had to have her own leg removed and replaced with the prosthetic.
2 CONC  One is that she was bit by a snake which required most of her leg to be removed in order to save her life. The other story is that she had been invited to a dance to which her father said "no". Apparently she and another girl bot
2 CONC h liked the same boy, and since Felicitas could not attend the dance the other girl thought she would get to be the center of the boy's attention. At the last moment Felicitas was permitted to attend the dance, to which the boy tu
2 CONC rned his attention to her, and when the two were dancing the other jealous girl came and stomped her shoe heel into the top of Felicitas' foot, causing serious injury and then infection, to which required that her leg be removed i
2 CONC n order to save her life. It is unknown which story is true.
2 CONT
2 CONT She and Desiderio had 8 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan (John) - b 1889 (circa) / d ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Josefina (twin) - b 1891 / d 1953
2 CONT
2 CONT Eloize (twin) - b 1891 / d 1965
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria - b 1893 (circa) / d ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Carmen - b 1903 / d 1980
2 CONT
2 CONT Paula ("Wanda") - b 1914 (circa) / d ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramon (Raymond) - b 1910 / d 1980
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel - b 1913 (circa) / d ?
2 CONT
2 CONT In her later years her daughter, Carmen, took care of her mother, Felicitas, until she passed away.  They are buried next to each other.
