1 OCCU Wealthy Rancher
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information provided by Joseph H Sanchez, 2nd great grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT Served on the Territorial government as a Republican  representative for Valencia County and also served as sheriff. Married two daughters of the Chavez line, had a son and daughter from the first sister and three daughters and a 
2 CONC son from the second sister. Well respected rancher of 300 head of cattle and 1,200 sheep. Owned a adobe hacienda and many acres in Valencia. Also owned a home in Albuquerque. My great great Aunt Alicia Sanchez, his daughter said t
2 CONC hat he died after falling off a horse. I am the proud owner of his ACME  work pocket watch, given to me by Aunt Alicia. I saw her open a box and after looking at a fine silver pocket watch, she gave me the simple work watch.  I al
2 CONC so have a printed paper from 1908 which announced his death and asked for the Valencia families to help rebuild a Capilla (small chapel) which had burned down in earlier years and was dedicated to San Jose. The chapel was rebuilt 
2 CONC on the Sanchez Hacienda in the hills of La Ladera de Valencia by Ubaldo Sanchez with the help of relatives and neighbors.The paper listed his grandparents and his father and from this information I was able to finish my family tre
2 CONC e in New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Jose Sanchez y Castillo his father served on the first territorial government as a Republican representative of Valencia County. My aunt Alicia said they both served as sheriff and tax collector of  Valencia County, New Mexic
2 CONC o.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Seems to be too many siblings (16) in this family from only one mother, but then again it could be true.
