1 OCCU Restaurant Owner and Cook 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marguerite Duran ran a restaurant out of her house near McNary, Arizona. A lot of her customers were Indians from the reservation. She was known for her delicious food. Her son Tony started a restaurant in Phoenix,
2 CONC  Arizona called the Teepee by borrowing $12,000 from his brother Albert to buy the land. Marguerite became one of the first cooks in the restaurant. The restaurant was named the Teepee and Mexican food as an acknowledgment to all 
2 CONC the years that Marguerite had cooked food for her Native American customers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT as told to Marcella Hoff by Gene Duran - Grandson of Maguerite Duran 
