1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The (Toledo OH) Blade of Friday, Nov. 29, 1974:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Deaths Elsewhere: Kit Carson, III'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Alamosa, Colorado (AP) - Kit Carson, III, one of eight grandchildren of frontier scout and guide Kit Carson, died Thursday after a brief illness. He was 91.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born June 30, 1883, at Fort Garland, Colorado, to Billy and Pascuela Tobin Carson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Carson was raised by his maternal grandfather, Tom Tobin, another western pioneer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Carson served as Conejos County clerk and recorder for many years and was active in other areas of local politics.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Lewiston Tribune of Thursday, Nov. 29, 1974
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kit Carson grandson dies at 91'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Alamosa, Colorado (AP) - Kit Carson III, one of eight grandchildren of famed frontier scout and guide Kit Carson, died Thursday after a brief illness. He was 91.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born June 30, 1883, at Fort Garland, Colorado, to Billy and Pascuela Tobin Carson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carson was raised by his maternal grandfather, Tom Tobin, another well-known western pioneer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carson served as Conejos County clerk and recorder for many years and was active in other areas of local politics.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his widow, Eloisa, a sister, a son, and two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were scheduled Monday morning at Sacred Heart Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Spokane Daily Chronicle of Saturday, Nov. 30, 1974
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Burial Set'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Alamosa, Colorado (UPI) - Kit Carson III, a grandson of his frontier Indian scout namesake, will be buried in this southern Colorado town Monday. Carson died Thursday at the age of 91.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
