1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Lucy may have married Carlos in La Plata, New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died of kidney Failure at the Hospital in Farmington, New Mexico.  Her physician stated when she died her father Remigio Valdez went into shock and died on the same day.
2 CONT It has been confirmed by my aunt Fidela and my aunt Maxine that they were both buried on the same day.  The place of death was Farmington, New Mexico.  The burial site is unknown.  If Greenlawn Cemetery was still in the area on th
2 CONC ese dates it is possible they were buried there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT My father Nestor Amadeo Valdez was approximately 12 years old when his father Remigio died.  Lucy's husband Carlos is not mentioned during the conversation.  No one seems to know what happened to him or if my tia Lucia had any chi
2 CONC ldren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy may have still been alive in 1926 she would have been circa 31 years old at her death.  My grandmother Juanita was about 18 years old when Lucy was born.  The Census data I found on my Grandmothers states she was about 16 yea
2 CONC rs old whenshe married.
