1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary from http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=armijo&GSfn=richard&GSby=1935&GSbyrel=before&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=70218632&df=all&  and   http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/elpasotimes/obituary
2 CONC .aspx?n=richard-armijo&pid=150856407
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT ARMIJO Richard Armijo, born January 5, 1930 in Las Cruces, New Mexico, passed away on May 4, 2011 at home surrounded by his family in El Paso, Texas. Richard was known for his sense of humor, generosity and devotion to family and 
2 CONC friends. An avid sports enthusiast, he enjoyed golf and fishing and was a devout Dallas Cowboys and UTEP Miners fan. He joined the National Guard and later served his country honorably as a Marine Sergeant in Korea for which he wa
2 CONC s awarded the Purple Heart. He retired from U.S. Customs after 35 years of service. He was preceded in death by his son Richard Michael Armijo and his first wife Rosela Armijo. He is survived by his loving wife of 25 years, Lupe A
2 CONC rmijo and his sons David Armijo and Albert Velarde; daughters Norma Cassell and Irma Vasquez; grand daughter Christy Craft and 11 more grand-children and 21 great grand children. Visitation will be held on Monday, May 9, 2011 from
2 CONC  5:00pm to 9:00pm with a Vigil service at 7:00pm at Hillcrest Funeral Home-Carolina. Mass of Christian Burial will be held on Tuesday, May 10, 2011 at 12:15pm at St. Pius X Catholic Church. Rite of Committal will follow at Ft. Bli
2 CONC ss National at 1:30pm at the West Shelter. Services under the direction of HILLCREST FUNERAL HOME 1060 N Carolina Dr. 598-3332
2 CONT
2 CONT .Published in El Paso Times from May 8 to May 10, 2011 
