1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1914 Death: 	Mar. 17, 2006
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary C. Vallejos, age 91, a lifelong resident of Adelino, peacefully joined our Lord and Savior, on Friday, March 17, surrounded by many of her loving family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was a member of Immaculate Conception Catholic Church in Tomé. She was a homemaker and fully devoted to her family. She was strong-willed and passed on many traits to all of her family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was preceded in death by her loving husband of 53 years, Fermin Vallejos; her parents, Jose Chavira and Loretta Gallegos; six brothers and three sisters. Mary was the last of the Chavira family.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her loving family, Felix and his wife, Helen, of Los Lunas, Viola Torrez of Los Lunas, Fred Sanchez and his wife, Bertha, of Barstow, Calif., Edwina Moya and her husband, Victor, of Albuquerque, Cathy Hernandez 
2 CONC of Barstow, Calif., Bertha Otero and her husband, Odelio, of Los Lunas, Gabriel Sanchez of Los Lunas, Henry Sanchez and his loving companion, Paula, of Albuquerque, Criselda Garcia and her loving companion, Eddie Otero, of Los Lun
2 CONC as and a granddaughter, Michelle Vallejos, who Mary and Fermin raised as their own; 31 grandchildren; 55 great-grandchildren; 23 great-great-grandchildren; and many loving nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held at Immaculate Conception Catholic Church beginning with a viewing on Sunday, March 19, from 5:30 to 6 p.m. followed by a rosary to be recited at 6 p.m. A final visitation will take place on Monday, March 20, 
2 CONC from 9:30 to 10 a.m. with the funeral Mass to be celebrated at 10 a.m. Interment will be held at Tomé Catholic Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers will be Juan Vallejos, Arthur Garcia, Brian Drake, Cindy Otero, Robert Sanchez, and Joe Moya. Romero Funeral Home, 609 N. Main St., Belen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Visit online register at www.romerofuneralhomenm.com.
