1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Errett was in the 200th Coast Artillery (Anti-Aircraft) New Mexico National Guard and moved into the newly formed 515th CA (AA) during the WWII invasion of the Philippines.  The 515th was sent to Manila to defend i
2 CONC t. He, along with tens of thousands of allied forces (mostly Filipino) were surrendered to the Japanese on April 9, 1942.  He spent a total of 3 1/2 years in prison camp - two in the Philippines and two in Japan.  He was among the
2 CONC  first ship load (November 1942) to be sent to labor camps in Japan.  I'm writing a book about the time and his experiences since I have his POW diaries.  
