1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rufino and his wife Cordie raised eight children.  He had two brothers Ben and Evaristo were always there for him and always helped him out. He had nieces and nephews that loved being around him and that looked up 
2 CONC to him.  Rufino was a good rancher,  and farmer.   He was a carpenter, wood worker, leather worker.   He was an avid Gardener.  He was a good Mechanic.    Rufino loved learning and enjoyed Math games.  Rufino was a good husband an
2 CONC d father.  He loved visits from his children and his grand children.
2 CONT
2 CONT What I remember the most when I hugged him was that he smelled of classic Old Spice and Velvet Pipe tabacco.  He gave great hugs and great advise.  He was an overcomer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Pa believed all his children were important they  were like the fingers of his hand all were important and dear to him.  Rufino said "no finger is more important then the other".
2 CONT
2 CONT I was impressed that my Grandpa would stand from a seating with one leg out.  Rufino had a steal plate in his leg.  He would find ways to over come his physical problems.  He was an awesome man.  who adored his life.  I enjoyed ti
2 CONC me with him.
