1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kathleen Ann CarsonAugust 3, 1947 – February 6, 2024
2 CONT Kathleen Ann Carson, 76, passed away peacefully at Crowley County Nursing Center in Ordway, CO on Tuesday, February 6, 2024. She was born, Sunday, August 3, 1947 in La Junta, Colorado to Kit & Alice (Mendyke) Carson.
2 CONT Kathleen graduated from La Junta High School as valedictorian in 1965. Kathleen was a Professional Engineer (PE) and through the years she continued her education earning degrees from Colorado College, University of Colorado, Colo
2 CONC rado State University, and the University of New Mexico. She also served in The United States Air Force with a rank of First Lieutenant.After retirement from the State of Arizona, Kathleen moved to Pueblo and finally back to La Ju
2 CONC nta. She took great interest in her nieces and nephews and especially enjoyed genealogy research.
2 CONT Kathleen is survived by her siblings, Glenn (Joanna) Carson of Nashville, TN; Rebecca Ray of Houston, TX; Christine Wynne of La Junta, CO; nieces & nephews, Christopher Carson; Kevin (Amber) Carson; Patricia (Dan Garner) Ray; Kati
2 CONC e Ray; Cyndi Ray; James (Erin) Ray; Kerri (Barrett) Bender; Jake (Naomi) Wynne; Tara (Brandon) Wynne-Neugebauer; along with several great nieces & nephews. She is preceded in death by her parents; nephew, Zachary Wynne; and brothe
2 CONC r in-law, Keith Wynne.
2 CONT There are no services planned at this time.
2 CONT Memorial donations can be made in Kathleen's name to the Otero Museum at www.oteromuseum.org or to Sangre De Cristo Hospice www.socohosice.org direct or through the funeral home. Online condolences may be made at www.PeacockFH.com
2 CONC . Peacock-Larsen Funeral Home & Arkansas Valley Crematory is in charge of arrangements.
