0 @N6000000002279635279@ NOTE Baptized on May 19, 1776 at Santa Cruz de la Canada, New Mexico.
1 CONT Padrinos were Francisco Pacheco and Margarita Pacheco.
0 @N6000000002279598322@ NOTE a.k.a. Juan Salvador Mestas in some record research.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the Mexican Census of 1845 (final census enumerated by the Mexican government for the Province of New Mexico) "Don" Salvador Mestas (30) and his wife "Dona" Bitoria Valdes (20) are enumerated along with 1-male child (age 1) and
1 CONC  1-female child (age 6 mos.) living in Abiquiu, New Mexico.
1 CONT ***675 males and 688 females are enumerated as living in Abiquiu.
1 CONT ***Don Eulogio Valdes, served as enumerator.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the 1850 United States Territorial Census, Salvador Mestas (age 36?) is living with his family in Rio Arriba Territory (County), New Mexico as enumerated on November 4, 1850.
1 CONT Wife: Antonia (20) Antonia Montoya?
1 CONT Son: Felipe (8)
1 CONT Daughters: Paula (6)
1 CONT    Manuela (4)
1 CONT    Maria (2)
1 CONT
1 CONT In the 1860 Census, Salvador (40) and his family are living in the Precinct of Fernando, Taos Territory (County), New Mexico. Post Office, Fernando de Taos. As enumerated on June 16, 1860.
1 CONT Wife: Biterba Valdez (38) Antonia Rosa Viterba de Valdes
1 CONT Son: Felipe Nerio (18)
1 CONT Daughters: Maria Paula (15)
1 CONT                    Maria Manuela (12)
1 CONT                    Dorotea (10)
1 CONT Son: Juan Maria (7)
1 CONT Daughters: Madalena (3)
1 CONT                    Maria Ygnacia (2 mos.)
1 CONT
1 CONT It is recorded in the Mestas Family Journal, written by Salvador's son Juan Maria in 1880, that the Mestas family first came into Las Animas County on April 15, 1866 from Chama, Rio Arriba, New Mexico.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the 1870 Census, Salvador (52) is living with his family in The Valley of the Purgatory River, East of Trinidad, Las Animas Territory (County), Colorado.  Post Office, Trinidad, Colorado Territory.  As enumerated on July 12, 18
1 CONC 70.
1 CONT Wife: Maria Antonia (50)
1 CONT Sons: Juan (15)
1 CONT           Jose (8)
1 CONT Daughter: Encarnacion (4)
1 CONT
1 CONT In the 1880 Census, Salvador is living with his family in Precinct #7, Las Animas County, Colorado as enumerated on June 17, 1880.
1 CONT Wife: Antonia 
1 CONT Son: Juan (25)
1 CONT Daughter: Encarnacion (14)
0 @N6000000002279602403@ NOTE Baptized on February 21, 1823 (5 days) in Abiquiu, New Mexico.
1 CONT Listed as "Vecinos de Chama."
1 CONT Padrinos: Francisco Antonio Gonzales.
1 CONT Madrina: Maria Dorotea Cruz.
0 @N6000000002279631852@ NOTE Baptized on January 7, 1840 (9 days) in Abiquiu, New Mexico.
1 CONT Listed as "Vecinos de Ojo Caliente."
1 CONT Padrino: Jose Maria Sanchez.
1 CONT Madrina: Maria Josefa Padilla.
