0 @N6000000002279631522@ NOTE Baptized on May 21, 1893 in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Colorado Marriage License #1267.
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Guillermo Lopez and Maria Mestas.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nicolasa Julia, named for her grandmother but used the name Julia, was the  first daughter born to Felipe Mestas and Eloisa Jaramillo. She married Louis G. Mendez and they had four children. They later divorced but remained friend
1 CONC s till their death. Julia moved to Denver in the 1940's and operated A & M Cleaners with the help of her daughters. Her daughters have told me that she was a wonderful mother, a superior cook and seamstress and a good woman  who w
1 CONC as always willing to help her family and extended family in time of need. She died of heart disease in 1968 and is buried at Mt. Olivet in Denver.
1 CONT As told to me by her daughters Helen and Carmen. 
1 CONT Source: Information from an unknown (Family Tree Maker) family tree contributor as posted on Ancestry.com, date unknown.
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried in 1968 at Mount Olivet Cemetery, Denver, Colorado.
0 @N6000000002279631533@ NOTE Baptized on April 21, 1896 in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Andres Sope and Doloritas Martinez.
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria, AKA Mary, was the second and last child born to Eloisa Jaramillo Mestas. In 1922, she married Jose N. Trujillo. Together they had four children. They ran the Denver Hotel in the 200 block of N. Commercial St. in Trinidad du
1 CONC ring the 1940's. They also lived in Walsenburg, CO. They weren't too close to family members for whatever reason. She did not even list her mother's name on her marriage document. In 1952, Jose died and she moved to NM. I heard th
1 CONC at she remarried and was later killed in an automobile accident in Talpa, NM. 
1 CONT Source: Information from an unknown (Family Tree Maker) family tree contributor as posted on Ancestry.com, date unknown. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried in Taos, New Mexico.
