0 @N6000000002279598008@ NOTE Baptized: October 10, 1920, Hoehne, Colorado by the Rev. J.B. Hugh, S.J.
1 CONT Padrinos: John Watson and Emma T. Watson.
1 CONT
1 CONT Served in World War II as part of the Army's 42nd Rainbow Division, Battery B, 402nd Field Artillery that was instrumental in the liberation of the Dachau Concentration Camp in Munich, Germany.
1 CONT Known as Danny Mestas in the military due to his registering for the military under the name Danny instead of Daniel.
1 CONT Danny was stationed at Camp Gruber, Oklahoma at one time during his military service.
1 CONT Daniel received his High School Diploma after returning from military service on December 30, 1949 in Hoehne, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married at Holy Trinity Catholic Church in Trinidad.
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Joe Max Lopez and Geneva (Sanchez) Lopez (Corina Sanchez's sister).
1 CONT Living at 1004 East First in Trinidad, Colorado at the time of his marriage.
1 CONT Daniel and Corina were living at 707 Elizabeth in Pueblo, Colorado at the time of the birth of their second son Daniel Phillip on June 4, 1955.
1 CONT Daniel was employed at the Pueblo Army Depot as a mechanical/electrical repair technician for 26 years.
1 CONT Was living at 111 South 3rd Street, LaSalle, Colorado where he died from Progressive Supranuclear Palsy at the age of 78 years.
1 CONT Buried: Imperial Memorial Gardens, 5450 Highway 78 West Pueblo, Pueblo, Colorado, 81005 with his wife Corina M. (Sanchez) Mestas.
0 @N6000000002279598086@ NOTE Left Hoehne, Colorado by 1940 to start work at Mt. San Rafael Hospital in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Lived on 619 Baltic St., Colorado Springs, Colorado, at one time, as indicated on her Social Security card.
1 CONT Gertrude was the Mestas and Montoya family member who was considered to be the historian of the family.  Along with her written accounts, she was also the person that everyone would told to ask a family related question of because
1 CONC  she seemed to know, all their was to know, about the family's  relationships, stories and events that made up the Mestas and Montoya's family history.  
1 CONT Buried:Trinidad Catholic Cemetery, Trinidad, Colorado near her mother Fructosa Mestas.
1 CONT Lived at 117 Benedicta Avenue, Trinidad, Colorado at the time of her death with her daughter Alice Vasquez.
